{{Quote|Supreme Chancellor Palpatine wants the tumor and all of the intel gathered sent to the Grand Republic Medical Facility on Coruscant.|Shaak Ti|<ref name="Fugitive">{{TCW|Fugitive}}</ref>}}
The '''Grand Imperial Medical Facility''', also known as the '''Grand Republic Medical Facility''' or '''Grand Medical Facility''', was a towering [[medcenter]] located on [[Coruscant]], the [[capital]] [[planet]] of the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Galactic Empire]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], the facility was used as a hospital to treat badly injured [[Republic Military]] personnel. In addition, the facility treated patients from across [[the galaxy]]. One such patient was the [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], who required [[Cybernetics|cybernetic]] reconstruction as a result of the injuries he [[Duel on Mustafar|sustained]] on [[Mustafar]]. [[Darth Sidious]], the secret persona of [[Supreme Chancellor]] Sheev Palpatine, used the facility as his retreat prior to [[Proclamation of the New Order|proclaiming]] himself [[Galactic Emperor]].

The facility remained in use during the [[Imperial Era]], although its secret role as Sidious' [[Sith]] haven was transferred to the [[Imperial Palace]]. During the [[Galactic Civil War]], Sidious brought Vader to the facility to be rebuilt following his [[Mission to Exegol|journey]] to [[Exegol]].

==Description==
{{Quote|The Grand Medical Facility is state-of-the-art.|Nala-Se|<ref name="Conspiracy">{{TCW|Conspiracy}}</ref>}}
[[File:Grand-Republic-Medical-Facility-SWCL.png|thumb|left|250px|During the Clone Wars, the Grand Republic Medical Facility was a fortified treatment center on Coruscant as well as Darth Sidious' Sith retreat.]]
The Grand Imperial Medical Facility<ref name="Master of Evil" /> was a [[Skyscraper|skyscraping]] tower and [[medcenter]] located in [[Imperial City]], a [[ecumenopolis]] and the [[planet]]ary [[capital]] of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Episode III" /> Under the Empire's predecessor, the [[Galactic Republic]], it was known as the Grand Republic Medical Facility<ref name="Fugitive" /> or Grand Medical Facility.<ref name="Conspiracy" /> The facility gained its new name, the "Grand Imperial Medical Facility," after the Republic [[proclamation of the New Order|transitioned]] into the Empire.<ref name="Master of Evil" />

The facility's lower levels were restructured to accommodate [[Darth Sidious]]' new [[Sith]] lair, and also housed a [[meditation chamber]] for the [[Sith Lord]]'s use. During the [[Clone Wars]], it was considered a high-value target because of its role as a Republic treatment center for [[Cloning|clones]] and other patients throughout [[the galaxy]]. As such, the facility was fortified with strong defense systems and powerful weaponry.<ref name="SWCL2016" /> Its security forces comprised the [[Imperial shock trooper|clone shock troopers]] of the [[Coruscant Guard]] and [[Supreme Chancellor]] Sheev Palpatine's [[Emperor's Royal Guard|Red Guards]].<ref name="Orders" />

==History==
===High Republic Era===
[[File:High Republic symbol.svg|thumb|right|250px|The Grand Republic Medical Facility was a Galactic Republic medcenter on Coruscant that dated back to the High Republic Era.]]
The Grand Republic Medical Facility was operated by the [[Galaxy|Galactic]] Republic since the [[time]] of the [[High Republic Era]]. The mentally distraught [[Jedi Knight]] [[Azlin Rell]] was brought to the facility in the aftermath of the [[Night of Sorrow|Battle of Dalna]] after Rell was traumatized by his encounter with a [[Shrikarai|Nameless]] during the battle. His carers remained unaware and confused by what he had encountered. Rell regularly experienced nightmares about his experience and began hurriedly writing a [[Azlin's journal|journal]] about the creatures. When the [[bounty hunter]] [[Vol Garat]] broke into his room to demand information on the Nameless, intending to use the creatures against the [[Jedi Order]], Rell remained preoccupied with the journal until the enraged bounty hunter knocked it away, ripping out several pages in the process.<ref name="Precedent">''[[The High Republic: The Edge of Balance: Precedent]]''</ref>

The commotion was heard by two nearby personnel, but Garat remained out of sight as they entered, leaving them to assume the mess was Rell's own doing after another nightmare. The officials decided that Rell needed rest instead of hospital care and thus transferred him to the [[Gravan Monastery]] on the [[moon]] [[Grava]], unaware that Garat had overheard their entire conversation. With less security at the monastery, Garat attacked Rell again on the moon, but was fought off by the [[Wookiee]] [[Jedi]] [[Arkoff]].<ref name="Precedent" />

===Clone Wars===
{{Quote|I recommend we do further tests on this tumor at the Jedi Temple to see if it is the cause of the problem.''"<br />"''Or even better, have the tumor sent to the Grand Republic Medical Facility here on Coruscant.|Shaak Ti and Sheev Palpatine|<ref name="Conspiracy" />}}
[[File:GrandRepublicMedicalFacility-TCWS06E04.png|thumb|left|250px|The ARC trooper known as Fives was taken to the Grand Republic Medical Facility on Coruscant at the behest of Supreme Chancellor Sheev Palpatine.]]
During the Clone Wars, [[clone trooper]] [[Tup]]'s malfunctioning [[behavioral modification biochip]] caused the clone to [[Battle of Ringo Vinda|kill]] [[Jedi General]] [[Tiplar]] in accordance with [[Order 66]].<ref name="The Unknown">{{TCW|The Unknown}}</ref> After the [[Advanced Recon Commando]] [[Fives]] discovered the biochips during his [[Escape from Tipoca City|investigation]] of Tup's actions on [[Ringo Vinda]], [[Jedi Master]] [[Shaak Ti]] and [[Doctor]] [[Nala Se]] conferred with Supreme Chancellor Sheev Palpatine, who suggested that they transport the biochips and Fives from [[Tipoca City]] on [[Kamino]] to the Grand Republic Medical Facility on Coruscant for further analysis. Nala Se supported Palpatine's proposal, stating that the facility was "state-of-the-art." Shaak Ti likewise heeded the chancellor's counsel, despite the [[Jedi High Council]]'s instructions to have the evidence delivered to them at the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on Coruscant.<ref name="Conspiracy" />

[[File:ShaakTiChasesFives-TCWS06E04.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Fives fled from the Grand Republic Medical Facility after attempting to assassinate Chancellor Palpatine.]]
Shaak Ti, Nala Se, and Fives arrived at the Grand Republic Medical Facility in a [[Nu-class attack/transport shuttle|''Nu''-class attack/transport shuttle]]. They were escorted into the facility by [[Vice Chair]] [[Mas Amedda]] and the clone shock troopers of the Coruscant Guard. After Fives voiced his suspicion that the biochip was responsible for Tup's execution of Tiplar, Chancellor Palpatine insisted on speaking with the ARC trooper in private. However, a confrontation ensued between Fives and the chancellor's [[bodyguard]]s. Shaak Ti returned in time to [[Force push|stop]] Fives from [[Blaster|shooting]] the chancellor with a [[DC-15A blaster carbine]]. The Jedi Master tried to capture Fives after Palpatine accused him of attempted murder, although the clone managed to [[Escape from the Grand Republic Medical Facility|escape]] from the facility. The Coruscant Guard launched a manhunt for the rogue ARC trooper, who was ultimately [[Mission to Level 1325|killed]] by [[Clone Commander]] [[Fox]] on [[Level 1325]] of Coruscant. Prior to his death, Fives tried to convince Jedi [[General]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]] that Chancellor Palpatine was involved in a [[Grand Plan|conspiracy]] against the Jedi Order, but Skywalker rejected Fives' claims because of his [[assassin]]ation attempt against the chancellor.<ref name="Orders" />

===Imperial Era===
[[File:ReturnToCoruscant-2020DarthVader12.png|thumb|left|250px|The Grand Republic Medical Facility became known as the Grand Imperial Medical Facility during the reign of the Galactic Empire.]]
Following the incident with Fives,<ref name="Orders" /> Palpatine moved his [[Darth Sidious' collection|collection]] of Sith [[Sith artifact|relics]] and artifacts from an [[Inquisitorius Headquarters|abandoned tower]] in [[The Works]] district to the Grand Republic Medical Facility, fearing they would be discovered by the Jedi.<ref name="SWCL2016" /> Unbeknownst to the Jedi at the time, Palpatine was the public persona of [[Darth]] Sidious, the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] who orchestrated the Clone Wars to gain more [[Politics|political]] power. After the rise of the Galactic Empire, a severely [[Duel on Mustafar|damaged]] Darth Vader was taken to the facility by the now-anointed [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] Palpatine. Utilizing a team of [[medical droid]]s, Sidious had his [[Sith apprentice]] surgically [[Cyborg|reconstructed]] using [[cybernetics]] and an [[Darth Vader's armor|armored suit]] to keep Vader alive.<ref name="Episode III" />

The Grand Imperial Medical Facility, as it was known under the Empire,<ref name="Master of Evil" /> was still operational at the time of the [[Galactic Civil War]]. Following Vader's [[Mission to Exegol|excursion]] to [[Exegol]], he returned with Sidious to Coruscant where his cybernetic body and [[armor]] were repaired in the Medical Facility.<ref name="Vader 12">[[Darth Vader (2020) 12|''Darth Vader'' (2020) 12]]</ref>

